public/

# The asset tree is a RELEASE ARTIFACT, not tracked content.
#
# It was Git LFS until 0.1.0-dev.1, and LFS is unavailable in the weftspun workspace: with
# `assets/** filter=lfs` in .gitattributes, checkout fails on a missing git-lfs binary and
# `repo sync` cannot initialize the work tree for this project at all. LFS is also invisible to
# `repo status`, which is the objection CLAUDE.md already raises against git submodules -- a
# second dependency mechanism the workspace's own tooling cannot see.
#
# Inlining the bytes was never possible: the largest object is 664 MB against GitHub's 100 MB
# per-file limit. Fetch them with `assets/fetch.sh`, following the same pattern
# `swing-twist-kusudama` uses for its Parquet datasets.
assets/*
!assets/fetch.sh
